Project Guidelines
- Use node 18.16.0 or higher.
- Always refer yarn.lock file first and package.json for dependencies.
- Consider src/styles directory for style refrences.
Code Style and Structure
- Write concise JavaScript following Standard.js rules.
- Use functional programming; avoid classes.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over duplication.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Structure files by exported component, subcomponents, helpers, and static content.
Component and State Management
- Use functional components and hooks (useState, useEffect).
- Use React-Redux and reduxtoolkit hooks (useSelector, useDispatch) for state management.
- Avoid inline function definitions within the render method.
UI and Styling
- Use Ant Design for component foundations.
- Style components using SCSS with BEM conventions.
- Use FontAwesome 6 <i> tags for icons.
- Organize SCSS files in a consistent structure (e.g., .module.scss).
  
Code Quality
- Enforce quality with ESLint (Airbnb style guide) and Prettier.
Error Handling and Validation
- Handle errors and edge cases early with guard clauses.
- Avoid unnecessary else statements; prioritize early returns.
- Log errors and provide user-friendly messages.
Security
- Sanitize user inputs; avoid dangerouslySetInnerHTML unless necessary and sanitized.